WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.733
- Hey, what's up?

00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:02.566
I'm Freddie.

00:00:02.566 --> 00:00:04.650
And today I'm gonna be
making peach cobbler.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.520
This recipe comes

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.370
from my best friend Tori's mom,

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.420
Cheryl Tucker,

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.020
lovingly known as Mama T.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.400
Mama T would kill me if
I used canned peaches,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.550
but peaches are not in season right now

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.280
and this is the only option.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.540
Usually, if I were to ask
her to make peach cobbler

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.680
not in season, she would refuse.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.640
So, when I first asked, she
was hesitant and I was like,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.510
she actually really may
not give me this recipe.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.430
And then, of course, a day later

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.990
she had it all written
out for me and ready to go

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.140
in the cutest way possible.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.440
I knew she was eventually
gonna give me something,

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.240
but I didn't think she was
gonna give me the exact recipe.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.670
This is the first time I'm
ever even really knowing

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.800
all that goes into it,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.650
because she kicks us out of the kitchen.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.150
So, there's a core group of
people that she makes it for,

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.230
and we don't even have to ask for it.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.430
If she knows we're gonna
be home or in the area

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.710
she will make sure that peach cobbler

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.690
is at her house waiting for us.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.710
It's great because

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.050
usually when you think about peach cobbler

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.120
you think of dessert,

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.040
but we'll just go over to her house

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.280
just to eat peach cobbler.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.500
Like, there's no dinner.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.160
Sometimes there's dinner to precede,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.880
but usually the peach
cobbler is the main dish.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.530
The best part about making the recipe

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.090
is seeing how simple it actually is

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.010
and that a majority of the ingredients

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.520
that she puts in are just love, laughter,

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.170
and just being an awesome mother figure.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.280
She has so much heart.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.240
She's so fun.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.650
She's like the most free-spirited
woman I've ever met.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.540
I've always said,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.070
I hope I'm the type of
woman and mom that she is.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.050
So, I don't go back home too often,

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.930
and cooking this really
brought me back to that place,

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:38.299
and I felt a really strong
connection to her and to home.

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:40.370
It smells very sweet,
it smells very peachy,

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.530
and it just smells like home.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.900
Mama T, thank you so much

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.900
for sharing your beloved recipe with me.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.760
I hope I made you proud!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.710
Much love in.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.620
Much love out.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.330
- [Man] Oh, yes!

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.830
(upbeat percussion music)

